Z||000010||batboy||03-24-2001||07:07 PM||||Here's my answer...it ain't worth the trouble. If you were to find a rod that was a little longer, that also didn't hit the bottom edge of cylinder as it spins on the crank, and it happened to be exactly the right journal size, then you still would have to find the right sized pistons with the correct pin height, which you probably can't find, thus would require having the pistons custom made, which of course would cost an arm and leg (or at least an internal organ). Wow, that's one long sentence. Anyway, for the lowly ol' Duke, it ain't worth the trouble, sorry to be so blunt.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||1
